[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139730,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Haemangioma of bone (HA-B), including epithelioid haemangioma (EH), is a benign vascular tumour infrequently involving the calvarium or facial bone including the orbit. It is genetically characterized by a fusion gene and can be locally aggressive.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139731,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9120/0 Haemangioma</p>\r\n<p>9125/0 Epithelioid haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139732,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E81.0Y &amp; XH5AW4 Neoplastic haemangioma of other specified site &amp; Haemangioma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>2E81.0Y &amp; XH10T4 Neoplastic haemangioma of other specified site &amp; Epithelioid haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139733,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> intraosseous haemangioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139734,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid haemangioma of bone (EH-B)</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139735,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The craniofacial skeleton including the orbit can be affected {33481536;16754225;28210401;31874384;33034932}. Lesions can be multifocal {34742485;31708630;33034932}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139736,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions grow slowly and are often asymptomatic. They can present as a swelling/mass and can cause a range of symptoms including pain, displacement (with proptosis and diplopia), ophthalmoparesis, and epiphora {33481536;16754225;31874384}.</p>\r\n<p>Imaging shows an expansile, often lobulated lesion with a polka-dot pattern that is hyperintense on MRI {31708630;34742485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139737,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>HA-Bs are relatively common and often incidental findings. They can be found at any age. Lesions often present in adulthood. The spine is the most common site followed by the craniofacial bones. The orbit is very rarely affected {28210401;31874384;34742485;34203801}.</p>\r\n<p>EH-B is rare, involving orbital bone exceptionally {31708630;28210401}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139738,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139739,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>HA-Bs are fusion gene&ndash;driven tumours, of which the genetic drivers are:</p>\r\n\r\nfor HA-B: <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>NFATC1</em> or <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>NFATC2 </em>{34081036;23480895;34742485}\r\nfor EH-B: <em>FOS </em>or <em>FOSB</em> rearrangements with variable partners (e.g. <em>ZFP36</em>::<em>FOSB</em>,<em> WWTR1</em>::<em>FOSB</em>,<em> FOS</em>::<em>LMNA</em>, and<em> FOS</em>::<em>VIM</em>) {32271190;33034932}.\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139740,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions are situated in the medullary cavity with a sponge-like haemorrhagic appearance and a delineated sclerotic border {34742485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139741,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>HA-B shows variable thin- and thick-walled vessels of different calibre without remarkable endothelial lining. A stromal reaction can be prominent. A vascular malformation can be difficult to differentiate.</p>\r\n<p>EH-B is distinguished by a lobular architecture of well-formed vessels with a pericytic cuff. In the centre of the lesion, the plump monomorphic epithelioid cells are sometimes tightly packed. There is a zonation pattern with peripheral maturation. The eosinophilic cytoplasm may possess vacuoles. Cellular atypia and necrosis can be confused with a malignant tumour {34742485;33034932;32271190}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry accentuates the organoid vasculature by highlighting the endothelial cells with CD31, CD34, ERG, and FLI1 staining. Pericytes&nbsp;/ smooth muscle cells express &alpha;SMA {34742485;31950476}.</p>\r\n<p>In EH-B, FOS or FOSB is positive {32271190}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139742,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139743,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>HA-B:<em> EWSR1</em>::<em>NFATC1 or EWSR1</em>::<em>NFATC2</em></p>\r\n<p>EH-B: <em>FOS</em> or <em>FOSB</em> rearrangement with variable fusion partners</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139744,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bone (orbit) as primary site; compatible radiology; for HA-B: thin-walled blood vessels lined by a single layer of non-atypical endothelial cells; for EH-B: large epithelioid endothelial cells with densely eosinophilic cytoplasm.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> detection of a fusion gene (see <em>Diagnostic molecular pathology</em>); for EH-B: lobular architecture with distinct vasoformation; FOS and FOSB positivity by immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139745,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139746,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is excellent. Recurrences are rare. Multifocality should not be interpreted as metastases {33481536;16754225;31874384;31708630;34742485}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]